Wrong (A): The loss is not deferred — it is permanently disallowed to the seller. While the buyer may benefit from Sec. 267(d) on a later sale, the seller never claims the loss.
Wrong (B): Section 267 does not convert the loss to a capital loss. The loss is simply disallowed entirely, regardless of whether it would have been ordinary or capital.
Wrong (C): There is no 50% limitation on related-party losses. Section 267(a)(1) disallows the entire loss, not a partial amount.$EXPL$
