  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 7872(a), forgone interest on below-market loans equals AFR interest minus actual interest: ($300,000 x 5% = $15,000) - ($300,000 x 1% = $3,000) = $12,000. This amount is treated as a constructive dividend to the shareholder under Sec. 301 and a deemed interest payment back to the corporation.
