-- Q4172: Owner-Entity Transactions [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 267(a) and Sec. 482, when a controlling shareholder sells property to a controlled corporation below FMV, the bargain element ($500,000 - $300,000 = $200,000) is treated as a constructive dividend to the shareholder. The corporation''s basis is $500,000 because the transaction is recharacterized as a purchase at $300,000 plus a $200,000 deemed capital contribution.
Wrong (A): The term "bargain sale" is incomplete. The $200,000 bargain element is specifically a constructive dividend to Emily, and Tau''s basis is stepped up to the full FMV of $500,000.
Wrong (B): The constructive dividend is to the shareholder (Emily), not to Tau Corp. The corporation receives property, while the shareholder is deemed to receive the bargain element as a dividend.
