Wrong (B): Exactly 50% ownership is not sufficient for related-party status under Sec. 267(b). The threshold requires more than 50% ownership, making the "exactly 50%" scenario not a related-party relationship.
Wrong (C): Two corporations with different, unrelated shareholders are not related parties under Sec. 267(b). Related-party status requires common ownership or family attribution exceeding the threshold.
